## Exit criteria

- [ ] Reproduce quoted-marker confusion with portable synthetic fixtures;
      cover duplicated leading separators, ordinary unmarked answers,
      truncated thinking, missing/refused reach, and markers in the body.
- [ ] Extract the actual final answer without rewriting its content or
      inventing worker/reach/tests declarations. State limitations where
      unstructured framing is ambiguous; avoid claims of cryptographic
      transport authenticity.
- [ ] Integrate equivalent portable regression coverage into the real
      harness tests, not only an Arena shim. Run the repository's applicable
      checks on the actual implementation.
- [ ] Provide an optional local replay of a supplied preserved raw artifact
      with its SHA checked; no dependency on volatile .tmp paths, private
      Arena checkout availability for default tests, or a new model call.
- [ ] Keep raw transcripts and launch links available through the monitoring
      archive; preserve original failure outcomes and distinguish parsing
      failure, unavailable response, and timeout in derived diagnostics.
- [ ] Respect memo 1382: no new online monitoring-record refusal, mandatory
      launch ceremony, parallel archive, index without its trigger, or
      automatic retry. Any necessary semantic review-contract change must
      be explicit rather than smuggled through normalization.

## Scope of this filing

Ticket and coordination only. No parser patch applied, no model/service
change, no new inference, no Arena review/gate relabelled and no publication
of private evidence. Arena 1184 remains held until its actual review and
admission requirements are satisfied under the then-current harness.
